{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "02K9", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-finite-locally-free}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:84fd2136b567575e75a6f7f7d350bf52cf2296e67c5ec19fd327257fa595543a", "source_text": "Finite locally free morphisms", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a8610f48e8442bb9187ddb4cdf50a7ff602921b8807a07dbf07463c4901d41f1", "unit_id": "tag:02K9:title"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "02K9", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{exercises-exercise-flat-not-projective}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1bd033f08934b22f82d3fe1d807645381089cd88a408d0f2efca72a39d7874e2", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn many papers the authors use finite flat morphisms when they really mean\nfinite locally free morphisms. The reason is that if the base is locally\nNoetherian then this is the same thing. But in general it is not, see\nExercises, Exercise <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:95d2258a8657eb493733df0db8cd37a99cf3d986cfe23e3768ec26b8a19167b7", "unit_id": "tag:02K9:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "02K9", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$f_*\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}_S$", "MATH_0006": "$f$", "MATH_0007": "$d$", "MATH_0008": "$f_*\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0009": "$d$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0003": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0003": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-finite-locally-free}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:4077b1df14b55d1858fede0d6062a37f105ff73e84d3a997d1d86f9f1cb67fd4", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:320e70cb92a5ac65dc8b7d7bad01dfcb0f8f55d737d0fd0fcc28c9ca21102781", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\nWe say <MATH_0002> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>finite locally free<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if <MATH_0003> is\naffine and <MATH_0004> is a finite locally\nfree <MATH_0005>-module. In this case we say <MATH_0006> is\nhas <TEXTITOPEN_0002>rank<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> or <TEXTITOPEN_0003>degree<TEXTITCLOSE_0003> <MATH_0007>\nif the sheaf <MATH_0008> is finite locally free of degree <MATH_0009>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:dca9d15ce8d02ac52f747284f564a57d186ac022e1ff5734bb445473ba8745aa", "unit_id": "tag:02KA:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "02K9", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$S_d$", "MATH_0004": "$f^{-1}(S_d) \\to S_d$", "MATH_0005": "$d$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:3b76ebcf5b11c476145722cfe87332c596658f122fa5d567c915a0f3455a496d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:fe38d5673e5c8e3f4f73e8793ee8a8c429cd81c788f57806f9339322f51ba180", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nNote that if <MATH_0001> is finite locally free then <MATH_0002> is the disjoint\nunion of open and closed subschemes <MATH_0003> such that <MATH_0004>\nis finite locally free of degree <MATH_0005>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1f1ff9b9564b3af80df6aac99ba834465ce98f24588dd651f54632c1ed1dd18c", "unit_id": "tag:02K9:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "02K9", "placeholders": {"ITEMCLOSE_0001": "]", "ITEMOPEN_0001": "\\item[", "MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$S$", "MATH_0005": "$f$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0005": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0006": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-finite-flat}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:dbc96a508923ec4b744e1a6c3a50ebc85b9feda0dc88237e6361098b6ac9e2f8", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:360364f8c02af82278830dc98b9bdebf7a5f5ab7a3f44937f7a168926ec2fa86", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\nThe following are equivalent:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0002> is finite locally free,\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0003> is finite, flat, and locally of finite presentation.\n<STRUCT_0004>\nIf <MATH_0004> is locally Noetherian these are also equivalent to\n<STRUCT_0005>\n<ITEMOPEN_0001>(3)<ITEMCLOSE_0001> <MATH_0005> is finite and flat.\n<STRUCT_0006>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2c25efd1893a97f32bbcdcd920aa93d465ddcf3a219de8feea4dbb00c9b5c78c", "unit_id": "tag:02KB:statement"}
